<title>HUNGARY: HUNGARY C/A GAP WIDENS BY $198 MLN IN FEBRUARY.</title>
<headline>HUNGARY C/A GAP WIDENS BY $198 MLN IN FEBRUARY.</headline>
<dateline>BUDAPEST 1997-05-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Hungary's current account deficit widened by</p>
<p>$198 million in February to an accumulated amount of $498 million, the National</p>
<p>Bank of Hungary said in a statement on Friday.</p>
<p>HUNGARY CURRENT ACCOUNT (in million dgllars)</p>
<p>			    Feb 97  Jan-Feb 97    Feb 96  Jan-Feb 96</p>
<p> Trade balance	    -229	-439	   -339	-641</p>
<p>  - Exports		1,348     2,807	    920     1,976</p>
<p>  - Imports		1,577     3,246	  1,258     2,617</p>
<p> Services and income	 7	0-86	    -56	-132</p>
<p>  - Tourism		   44	  69	     40	  52</p>
<p>- Capital investment</p>
<p>    income		   -40	-155	   -114	-225</p>
<p>- Other current</p>
<p>    payments		  03	   0	     17	  42</p>
<p> Unrequited transfers     24	  27	     82	 165</p>
<p> Current account	  -198	-498	   -313	-607</p>
<p>Foreign direct capital</p>
<p>  investments		131	 215	    128	 347</p>
<p>NOTE - Central bank trade figures are based on cash flow data. (Ministry of</p>
<p>Industry, Trade and Tourism trade figures are based gn customs</p>
<p>statistics.</p>
<p>-- Budapest newsroom (36 1) 327 4040</p>
</text>
